Today marks Day 29 of my 120-day data analytics journey, and I officially started learning SQL.

To put my skills into practice, I began working on a guided project where I step into the role of a data analyst at a startup. The product team is considering launching a Kickstarter campaign, and my task is to analyze historical Kickstarter data to understand what makes campaigns succeed or fail.

This project will involve exploring campaign categories, funding goals, number of backers, and pledged amounts  all using SQL to uncover meaningful insights that could influence real business decisions.

It’s exciting to move from spreadsheets into querying databases directly. Every new tool makes the data story clearer.
